      "attestations": [
        {
          "text": "LI T'ien-fu 李天馥 (T. 湘北, H. 容齋) Mar. 12, 1635–1699, Dec. 5; official, was originally from Ho-fei, Anhwei, but registered in the examinations as a native of Yung-ch'êng, Honan. Receiving his chin-shih in 1658, he was made a corrector in 1661, and became sub-chancellor of the Grand Secretariat in 1677.",
